{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Deliver me, I pray, from the hand of my brother, from the hand of Esau.</b> For he does not deal with me as a brother but as Esau the wicked." "<b>And it is possible</b> to interpret that he prayed for that hour and for the generations: 'from the hand of my brother' — for that hour; 'from the hand of Esau' — for the generations. And this is as written (Genesis 27:22): ״והידים ידי עשו״ — 'and the hands are the hands of Esau' — and concerning him David, peace be upon him, prayed (Psalms 10:15): ״שבור זרוע רשע״ — 'break the arm of the wicked.'" "<b>For I fear him.</b> Because he has no mercy. And so the prophet, peace be upon him, said (Amos 1:11): ״על רדפו בחרב אחיו ושחת רחמיו״ — 'because he pursued his brother with the sword and destroyed his compassions.' <b>Lest he come and strike me</b> — and strike afterwards — <b>mother upon children.</b>" "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'Lest he come and strike me' — 'mother upon children.' Now, was it not commanded in the Torah (Leviticus 22:28): ״אותו ואת בנו לא תשחטו ביום אחד״ — 'it and its young you shall not slaughter on one day' — and concerning birds it is written (Deuteronomy 22:6): ״לא תקח האם על בנים״ — 'you shall not take the mother upon the young' — and he is destined to fulfill (Hosea 10:14): ״אם על בנים רוטשה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {2 "Comment [2] and comment [3] both conclude with the phrase אם על בנים; comment [2] appears to gloss it as 'mother upon children' (cf. Deut. 22:6), while comment [3] reads it as a phrase from Hoshea 10:14. Translated hyper-literally as the text stands.", 3 "The citation (דברים כו) lacks a verse number; resolved to Deuteronomy 22:6, the verse containing לא תקח האם על בנים."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:10.240710629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}